      "id": "CRL-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Lifting the power character to cyclotomic integers",
      "anchor": "inputs-character-lift",
      "statement": "At a degree-one prime above p prime to M, reducing a primitive Mth root preserves its order; M divides p−1. For h=(p−1)/M there is a multiplicative character, zero at zero, of exact order M, with χ(x)^M=1 and πχ(x)=x^h on the units.",
      "hypotheses": "K=ℚ(ζ_M); chosen prime ideal of absolute norm p, p prime, M≥1, gcd(p,M)=1. In the more general character lemma only an integral domain and primitive roots on both sides of π are used.",
      "definitions": [
        "cyclotomic polynomial",
        "absolute norm of a prime ideal",
        "multiplicative character",
        "order of a root of unity"
      ],
